#=GF RM   30423142
#=GF RT   miRBase: from microRNA sequences to function.
#=GF RA   Kozomara A, Birgaoanu M, Griffiths-Jones S
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res. 2019;47:D155.
#=GF CC   This family represents the microRNAs (miRNA) let-7 and mir-98. let-7 was
#=GF CC   identified from a study of developmental timing in C. elegans [1], and was
#=GF CC   later shown to be part of a much larger class of non-coding RNAs termed
#=GF CC   miRNAs [2]. Both miRNAs let-7 and mir-98 have now been predicted or
#=GF CC   experimentally confirmed in a wide range of species (MIPF:MIPF000002).
#=GF CC   miRNAs are transcribed as ~70nt precursors (modelled here) and
#=GF CC   subsequently processed by the Dicer enzyme to give a ~22nt product. The
#=GF CC   extents of the hairpin precursors are not generally known and are
#=GF CC   estimated based on hairpin prediction. The products are thought to have
#=GF CC   regulatory roles through complementarity to mRNA. The involvement of Dicer
#=GF CC   in miRNA processing suggests a relationship with the phenomenon of RNA
#=GF CC   interference. This family also includes the miR-98 precursor from human,
#=GF CC   which may be a let-7 homologue. The pre-miRNA structure of let-7 has been
#=GF CC   reported in complex with Dicer-TRBP [3]. Family represents miRNA precursor
#=GF CC   let-7 imported from miRBase [4].
#=GF WK   let-7_microRNA_precursor
#=GF SQ   64


