#=GF DR   GO; 0006364; rRNA processing;
#=GF DR   GO; 0000171; ribonuclease MRP activity;
#=GF DR   GO; 0000172; ribonuclease MRP complex;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   7678563
#=GF RT   Secondary structure of RNase MRP RNA as predicted by phylogenetic
#=GF RT   comparison.
#=GF RA   Schmitt ME, Bennett JL, Dairaghi DJ, Clayton DA
#=GF RL   FASEB J 1993;7:208-213.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   12088147
#=GF RT   Phylogenetic analysis of the structure of RNase MRP RNA in yeasts.
#=GF RA   Li X, Frank DN, Pace N, Zengel JM, Lindahl L
#=GF RL   RNA 2002;8:740-751.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   16087735
#=GF RT   Identification and analysis of ribonuclease P and MRP RNA in a broad range
#=GF RT   of eukaryotes.
#=GF RA   Piccinelli P, Rosenblad MA, Samuelsson T
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res. 2005;33:4485-4495.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   16083861
#=GF RT   Secondary structure probing of the human RNase MRP RNA reveals the
#=GF RT   potential for MRP RNA subsets.
#=GF RA   Walker SC, Avis JM
#=GF RL   Biochem Biophys Res Commun. 2005;335:314-321.
#=GF RN   [5]
#=GF RM   16998185
#=GF RT   Inventory and analysis of the protein subunits of the ribonucleases P and
#=GF RT   MRP provides further evidence of homology between the yeast and human
#=GF RT   enzymes.
#=GF RA   Rosenblad MA, Lopez MD, Piccinelli P, Samuelsson T
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res. 2006;34:5145-5156.
#=GF CC   RNase MRP is an enzymatically active ribonucleoprotein with two distinct
#=GF CC   roles in eukaryotes. In mitochondria it plays a direct role in the
#=GF CC   initiation of mitochondrial DNA replication. In the nucleus it is involved
#=GF CC   in precursor rRNA processing, where it cleaves the internal transcribed
#=GF CC   spacer 1 between 18S and 5.8S rRNAs. Despite distinct functions, RNase MRP
#=GF CC   has been shown to be evolutionarily related to RNase P. Like eukaryotic
#=GF CC   RNase P, RNase MRP is not catalytically active without associated protein
#=GF CC   subunits.
#=GF WK   RNase_MRP
#=GF SQ   66


