#=GF CL   CL00013
#=GF DR   SO; 0000274; snRNA;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   11864590
#=GF RT   Transcription: surprising role for an elusive small nuclear RNA.
#=GF RA   Blencowe BJ
#=GF RL   Curr Biol 2002;12:R147-149.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   1646389
#=GF RT   Structural analyses of the 7SK ribonucleoprotein (RNP), the most abundant
#=GF RT   human small RNP of unknown function.
#=GF RA   Wassarman DA, Steitz JA
#=GF RL   Mol Cell Biol 1991;11:3432-3445.
#=GF CC   7SK was discovered as an abundant small nuclear RNA in the mid-70s but a
#=GF CC   possible function has only recently been suggested [1]. Two independent
#=GF CC   studies have found that 7SK RNA binds the CDK9/cyclin T complex (known as
#=GF CC   elongation factor P-TEFb). P-TEFb activates transcription by
#=GF CC   phosphorylating the C-terminal domain of RNA polymerase II. This process
#=GF CC   is negatively regulated by the 7SK RNP. The secondary structure of 7SK RNA
#=GF CC   shown here was proposed by Wasserman and Steitz on the basis of chemical
#=GF CC   modification and enzymatic cleavage experiments [2]. This family contains
#=GF CC   a number of annotated pseudogenes and 7SK derived repeats. The threshold
#=GF CC   is artificially high to minimise the pseudogene count.
#=GF WK   7SK_RNA
#=GF SQ   45


