#=GF AC   RF00166
#=GF ID   PrrB_RsmZ
#=GF DE   PrrB/RsmZ RNA family
#=GF AU   Filiatrault M
#=GF AU   Gardner P; 0000-0002-7808-1213
#=GF SE   Filiatrault M
#=GF SS   Predicted; Filiatrault M, Gardner P
#=GF GA   38.00
#=GF TC   39.40
#=GF NC   37.30
#=GF TP   Gene; sRNA;
#=GF BM   cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB   cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -E 1000 -Z 549862.597050 CM SEQDB
#=GF CL   CL00106
#=GF DR   SO; 0000655; ncRNA;
#=GF DR   GO; 0006401; RNA catabolic process;
#=GF DR   GO; 0006109; regulation of carbohydrate metabolic process;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   10869066
#=GF RT   A regulatory RNA (PrrB RNA) modulates expression of secondary metabolite
#=GF RT   genes in Pseudomonas fluorescens F113.
#=GF RA   Aarons S, Abbas A, Adams C, Fenton A, O'Gara F
#=GF RL   J Bacteriol 2000;182:3913-3919.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   28400281
#=GF RT   The Pseudomonas transcriptional regulator AlgR controls LipA expression
#=GF RT   via the noncoding RNA RsmZ in Pseudomonas protegens Pf-5.
#=GF RA   Li M, Yan J, Yan Y
#=GF RL   Biochem Biophys Res Commun. 2017;487:173-180.
#=GF CC   PrrB RNA is able to phenotypically complement gacS and gacA mutants and is
#=GF CC   itself regulated by the GacS-GacA two-component signal transduction system
#=GF CC   [1]. Inactivation of the prrB gene in Pseudomonas fluorescens F113
#=GF CC   resulted in a significant reduction of 2, 4-diacetylphloroglucinol (Phl)
#=GF CC   and hydrogen cyanide (HCN) production, while increased metabolite
#=GF CC   production was observed when prrB was overexpressed [1]. The prrB gene
#=GF CC   sequence contains a number of imperfect repeats of the consensus sequence
#=GF CC   5'-AGGA-3', and sequence analysis predicted a complex secondary structure
#=GF CC   featuring multiple putative stem-loops with the consensus sequences
#=GF CC   predominantly positioned at the single-stranded regions at the ends of the
#=GF CC   stem-loops. This structure is similar to the CsrB and RsmB regulatory RNAs
#=GF CC   Rfam:RF00018 [1], suggesting this RNA also interacts with a CsrA-like
#=GF CC   protein.
#=GF WK   PrrB/RsmZ_RNA_family
#=GF SQ   37


