#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   12787499
#=GF RT   Riboswitches Control Fundamental Biochemical Pathways in Bacillus subtilis
#=GF RT   and Other Bacteria.
#=GF RA   Mandal M, Boese B, Barrick JE, Winkler WC, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Cell 2003;113:577-586.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   14718920
#=GF RT   Adenine riboswitches and gene activation by disruption of a transcription
#=GF RT   terminator.
#=GF RA   Mandal M, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Nat Struct Mol Biol 2004;11:29-35.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   15549109
#=GF RT   Structure of a natural guanine-responsive riboswitch complexed with the
#=GF RT   metabolite hypoxanthine.
#=GF RA   Batey RT, Gilbert SD, Montange RK
#=GF RL   Nature. 2004;432:411-415.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   23842498
#=GF RT   Three-state mechanism couples ligand and temperature sensing in
#=GF RT   riboswitches.
#=GF RA   Reining A, Nozinovic S, Schlepckow K, Buhr F, Furtig B, Schwalbe H
#=GF RL   Nature. 2013;499:355-359.
#=GF CC   Riboswitches are metabolite binding domains within certain messenger RNAs
#=GF CC   that serve as precision sensors for their corresponding targets.
#=GF CC   Allosteric rearrangement of mRNA structure is mediated by ligand binding,
#=GF CC   and this results in modulation of gene expression. A class of riboswitches
#=GF CC   that selectively recognises guanine and becomes saturated at
#=GF CC   concentrations as low as 5 nM. In Bacillus subtilis, this mRNA motif is
#=GF CC   located on at least five separate transcriptional units that together
#=GF CC   encode 17 genes that are mostly involved in purine transport and purine
#=GF CC   nucleotide biosynthesis. It has also been shown that some members of this
#=GF CC   family are specific for adenine instead. Hence this family are termed
#=GF CC   purine riboswitches.
#=GF WK   Purine_riboswitch
#=GF SQ   133


