#=GF CC   (MIPF:MIPF000006). This miRNA family appears to be vertebrate specific and
#=GF CC   members of this family have been predicted or experimentally validated in
#=GF CC   a wide range of vertebrate species (MIPF:MIPF0000006). miR-16 and miR-15a
#=GF CC   are clustered within 0.5 kb at 13q14 in human, a region shown to be
#=GF CC   deleted or down-regulated in more than half of B cell chronic lymphocytic
#=GF CC   leukaemias (CLL) [1]. The hairpin precursors (represented here) are
#=GF CC   predicted based on base pairing and cross-species conservation -- their
#=GF CC   extents are not known. In this case the mature sequence is excised from
#=GF CC   the 5' arm of the hairpin.
#=GF WK   mir-16_microRNA_precursor_family
#=GF SQ   12


