#=GF AC   RF00380
#=GF ID   M-box
#=GF PI   ykoK;
#=GF DE   M-box riboswitch (ykoK leader)
#=GF AU   Moxon SJ; 0000-0003-4644-1816
#=GF AU   Ontiveros-Palacios N; 0000-0001-8457-4455
#=GF SE   Barrick JE, Breaker RR
#=GF SS   Predicted; Barrick JE, Breaker RR
#=GF GA   44.00
#=GF TC   44.10
#=GF NC   36.90
#=GF TP   Cis-reg; riboswitch;
#=GF BM   cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB   cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 742849.287494 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR   SO; 0000233; mature_transcript;
#=GF DR   GO; 0010468; regulation of gene expression;
#=GF DR   GO; 0032026; response to magnesium ion;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   15096624
#=GF RT   New RNA motifs suggest an expanded scope for riboswitches in bacterial
#=GF RT   genetic control.
#=GF RA   Barrick JE, Corbino KA, Winkler WC, Nahvi A, Mandal M, Collins J, Lee M,
#=GF RA   Roth A, Sudarsan N, Jona I, Wickiser JK, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A 2004;101:6421-6426.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   17803910
#=GF RT   Structure and mechanism of a metal-sensing regulatory RNA.
#=GF RA   Dann CE 3rd, Wakeman CA, Sieling CL, Baker SC, Irnov I, Winkler WC
#=GF RL   Cell. 2007;130:878-892.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   21315082
#=GF RT   Insights into metalloregulation by M-box riboswitch RNAs via structural
#=GF RT   analysis  of manganese-bound complexes.
#=GF RA   Ramesh A, Wakeman CA, Winkler WC
#=GF RL   J Mol Biol. 2011;407:556-570
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   20023416
#=GF RT   Magnesium-sensing riboswitches in bacteria.
#=GF RA   Ramesh A, Winkler WC
#=GF RL   RNA Biol. 2010;7:77-83.
#=GF CC   M-box riboswitch, also know as ykoK leader is described as a
#=GF CC   metaloregulatory RNA that sense divalent metals and function as a genetic
#=GF CC   control element of genes related to divalent metal transport in bacteria.
#=GF CC   It was first reported upstream of the B.subtilis ykoK gene and genes with
#=GF CC   related functions in other bacteria [1]. The structure of the M-box was
#=GF CC   first reported in PDB 2QBZ [2], as a structure of three parallel helices,
#=GF CC   where P3 and P4 helixes form a coaxial stack that folds alongside P2 and
#=GF CC   P5. Six Mg2+ recognition sites were reported in 2QBZ, while in a second
#=GF CC   structure report in PDB 3PDR, the authors report another three sites of
#=GF CC   Mn2+ bound that been predicted from phosphorothioate substitution
#=GF CC   experiments and six more additional Mn2+ proposed from the analysis of the
#=GF CC   anomalous density in the sequence [3]. Phylogenetic analysis of the
#=GF CC   distribution of M-box RNAs across bacterial genomes revealed that M-box
#=GF CC   riboswitches are most often employed for the regulation of Mg2+
#=GF CC   transporter genes [4]
#=GF WK   ykoK_leader
#=GF **   seedtax: Bacteria; unclassified sequences
#=GF SQ   159


