#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   9300054
#=GF RT   Structural probing and mutagenic analysis of the stem-loop required for
#=GF RT   Escherichia coli dnaX ribosomal frameshifting: programmed efficiency of
#=GF RT   50%.
#=GF RA   Larsen B, Gesteland RF, Atkins JF
#=GF RL   J Mol Biol 1997;271:47-60.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   9209069
#=GF RT   Conservation of the Escherichia coli dnaX programmed ribosomal frameshift
#=GF RT   signal in Salmonella typhimurium.
#=GF RA   Blinkova A, Burkart MF, Owens TD, Walker JR
#=GF RL   J Bacteriol 1997;179:4438-4442.
#=GF CC   This family represents a ribosomal frameshifting element found in the mRNA
#=GF CC   of the dnaX gene in E. coli. The dnaX gene has two encoded products tau
#=GF CC   and gamma which are produced in a 1:1 ratio. The gamma protein is
#=GF CC   synthesised due to programmed frameshifting and is shorter than tau. The
#=GF CC   two products of the dnaX gene are DNA polymerase III subunits [1,2].
#=GF WK   DnaX_ribosomal_frameshifting_element
#=GF SQ   5


