#=GF AC   RF00442
#=GF ID   ykkC-yxkD
#=GF DE   Guanidine-I riboswitch
#=GF AU   Moxon SJ; 0000-0003-4644-1816
#=GF AU   Ontiveros-Palacios N; 0000-0001-8457-4455
#=GF SE   Barrick JE, Breaker RR
#=GF SS   Predicted; Barrick JE, Breaker RR
#=GF GA   63.00
#=GF TC   63.00
#=GF NC   62.90
#=GF TP   Cis-reg; riboswitch;
#=GF BM   cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB   cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 742849.287494 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR   SO; 0000233; mature_transcript;
#=GF DR   GO; 0010468; regulation of gene expression;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   15096624
#=GF RT   New RNA motifs suggest an expanded scope for riboswitches in bacterial
#=GF RT   genetic control.
#=GF RA   Barrick JE, Corbino KA, Winkler WC, Nahvi A, Mandal M, Collins J, Lee M,
#=GF RA   Roth A, Sudarsan N, Jona I, Wickiser JK, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A 2004;101:6421-6426.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   27989440
#=GF RT   Metabolism of Free Guanidine in Bacteria Is Regulated by a Widespread
#=GF RT   Riboswitch  Class.
#=GF RA   Nelson JW, Atilho RM, Sherlock ME, Stockbridge RB, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Mol Cell. 2017;65:220-230.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   28096518
#=GF RT   Structural basis for guanidine sensing by the ykkC family of riboswitches.
#=GF RA   Battaglia RA, Price IR, Ke A
#=GF RL   RNA. 2017;23:578-585.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   28017522
#=GF RT   Structural Basis for Ligand Binding to the Guanidine-I Riboswitch.
#=GF RA   Reiss CW, Xiong Y, Strobel SA
#=GF RL   Structure. 2017;25:195-202.
#=GF RN   [5]
#=GF RM   34257148
#=GF RT   An uncommon [K(+)(Mg(2+))2] metal ion triad imparts stability and
#=GF RT   selectivity to  the Guanidine-I riboswitch.
#=GF RA   Trachman RJ 3rd, Ferre-D'Amare AR
#=GF RL   RNA. 2021;27:1257-1264.
#=GF CC   This family represents a conserved RNA structure found upstream of the
#=GF CC   ykkC and yxkD genes in Bacillus subtilis and related genes in other
#=GF CC   bacteria. The function of this family is unclear although it has been
#=GF CC   suggested that it may function to switch on efflux pumps and
#=GF CC   detoxification systems in response to harmful environmental molecules [1].
#=GF CC   The Thermoanaerobacter tengcongensis sequence EMBL:AE013027 overlaps with
#=GF CC   Rfam:RF00167 suggesting that the two riboswitches may work in conjunction
#=GF CC   to regulate the upstream gene which codes for Swiss:Q8RC62, a member of
#=GF CC   Pfam:PF00860 (Moxon SJ, pers. obs.). Nelson [2] showed that this
#=GF CC   riboswitch senses and responds to guanidine and it was renamed Guanidine-I
#=GF CC   riboswitch. Furthermore, they demonstrated that bacteria are capable of
#=GF CC   endogenously producing guanidine and the riboswitch controls genes whose
#=GF CC   products are involved in modification or pumping out guanidine as a toxic
#=GF CC   compound from bacteria. Crystal structures of the riboswitch bound to the
#=GF CC   ligand have also been determined in PDB 5T83, 5U3G and 7MLW [3][4].
#=GF WK   YkkC-yxkD_leader
#=GF SQ   100


