#=GF RT   A small bacterial RNA regulates a putative ABC transporter.
#=GF RA   Antal M, Bordeau V, Douchin V, Felden B
#=GF RL   J Biol Chem. 2005;280:7901-7908.
#=GF CC   This family represents a bacterial non-coding RNA called RydC. RydC is
#=GF CC   thought to regulate an mRNA, yejABEF which encodes an ABC transporter
#=GF CC   protein. RydC is known to bind the protein Hfq which causes a
#=GF CC   conformational change in the RNA molecule. The Hfq/RydC complex is then
#=GF CC   thought to bind to the target mRNA and induce its degradation [1].
#=GF WK   RydC_RNA
#=GF SQ   5


