#=GF ID   Corona_FSE
#=GF DE   Coronavirus frameshifting stimulation element
#=GF AU   Moxon SJ; 0000-0003-4644-1816
#=GF AU   Nawrocki E; 0000-0002-2497-3427
#=GF AU   Ontiveros-Palacios N; 0000-0001-8457-4455
#=GF SE   PMID:15680415
#=GF SS   Published; PMID:15680415
#=GF GA   46.00
#=GF TC   46.40
#=GF NC   33.10
#=GF TP   Cis-reg; frameshift_element;
#=GF BM   cmbuild -F CM SEED
#=GF CB   cmcalibrate --mpi CM
#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 742849.287494 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR   SO; 0000233; mature_transcript;
#=GF DR   GO; 0075523; viral translational frameshifting;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   15680415
#=GF RT   Programmed ribosomal frameshifting in decoding the SARS-CoV genome.
#=GF RA   Baranov PV, Henderson CM, Anderson CB, Gesteland RF, Atkins JF, Howard MT
#=GF RL   Virology 2005;332:498-510.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   32743589
#=GF RT   Cryo-electron Microscopy and Exploratory Antisense Targeting of the 28-kDa
#=GF RT   Frameshift Stimulation Element from the SARS-CoV-2 RNA Genome.
#=GF RA   Zhang K, Zheludev IN, Hagey RJ, Wu MT, Haslecker R, Hou YJ, Kretsch R,
#=GF RA   Pintilie GD, Rangan R, Kladwang W, Li S, Pham EA, Bernardin-Souibgui C,
#=GF RA   Baric RS, Sheahan TP, D Souza V, Glenn JS, Chiu W, Das R
#=GF RL   bioRxiv. 2020; [Epub ahead of print]
#=GF CC   This family represents a conserved stem-loop found in Coronaviruses which
#=GF CC   can promote ribosomal frameshifting. This family interacts with a
#=GF CC   downstream region to form a pseudoknot structure, the region varies
#=GF CC   according to the virus but pseudoknot formation is known to stimulate
#=GF CC   frameshifting. In the classical situation a sequence 32nt downstream of
#=GF CC   the stem is complementary to part of the loop. In other Coronaviruses
#=GF CC   however, there is another stem loop structure around 150nt downstream that
#=GF CC   can interact with this family to form kissing stem loops and stimulate
#=GF CC   frameshifting [1]. The structure of coronavirus frameshifting has been
#=GF CC   reported in PDB 6XRZ [2]. Revised in 2020-2021 to expand the seed
#=GF CC   alignment.
#=GF WK   Coronavirus_frameshifting_stimulation_element
#=GF SQ   50


