#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 742849.287494 CM SEQDB
#=GF CL   CL00129
#=GF DR   GO; 0039694; viral RNA genome replication;
#=GF DR   SO; 0000205; three_prime_UTR;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   19004935
#=GF RT   Structural and functional studies of the promoter element for dengue virus
#=GF RT   RNA replication.
#=GF RA   Lodeiro MF, Filomatori CV, Gamarnik AV
#=GF RL   J Virol. 2009;83:993-1008.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   21994804
#=GF RT   Functional RNA elements in the dengue virus genome.
#=GF RA   Gebhard LG, Filomatori CV, Gamarnik AV
#=GF RL   Viruses. 2011;3:1739-1756.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   33953197
#=GF RT   Structures of flavivirus RNA promoters suggest two binding modes with NS5
#=GF RT   polymerase.
#=GF RA   Lee E, Bujalowski PJ, Teramoto T, Gottipati K, Scott SD, Padmanabhan R,
#=GF RA   Choi KH
#=GF RL   Nat Commun. 2021;12:2530.
#=GF CC   Flavivirus stem-loop A (SLA) is a secondary structure present in the 5
#=GF CC   prime untranslated (5'-UTR) region of viruses of the genus Flavivirus. SLA
#=GF CC   structure was first proposed from enzymatic and chemical probing methods
#=GF CC   [1,2] afterwards the 3D structure of Dengue (PDB:7LYF) and Zika (PDB:5U0B)
#=GF CC   SLA viruses were reported [3]. SLA interacts with the nonstructural
#=GF CC   protein 5 (NS5), where SLA functions as a promoter for viral RNA synthesis
#=GF CC   by NS5 polymerase. The SLA secondary structure includes a bottom stem-loop
#=GF CC   (previously reported as SL1 and SL2), a top stem-loop (previously reported
#=GF CC   as SL3 and TL) and a side-loop (previously proposed as side SL). The side
#=GF CC   SL variate in length between flaviviruses (Tick-borne flaviviruses present
#=GF CC   a side SL >40nt), despite the lack of sequence conservation, deletion of
#=GF CC   the side SL abolish replication in Dengue virus. It is proposed that the
#=GF CC   side SL is essential to maintain the overall fold of Flavivirus SLA [3].
#=GF WK   Flavivirus
#=GF SQ   11



