#=GF DR   GO; 0005693; U12 snRNP;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   10199569
#=GF RT   Conservation of functional features of U6atac and U12 snRNAs between
#=GF RT   vertebrates and higher plants.
#=GF RA   Shukla GC, Padgett RA
#=GF RL   RNA 1999;5:525-538.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   9149533
#=GF RT   Pre-mRNA splicing: the discovery of a new spliceosome doubles the
#=GF RT   challenge.
#=GF RA   Tarn WY, Steitz JA
#=GF RL   Trends Biochem Sci 1997;22:132-137.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   11864616
#=GF RT   The divergent U12-type spliceosome is required for pre-mRNA splicing and
#=GF RT   is essential for development in Drosophila.
#=GF RA   Otake LR, Scamborova P, Hashimoto C, Steitz JA
#=GF RL   Mol Cell 2002;9:439-446.
#=GF CC   The U12 small nuclear (snRNA), together with U4atac/U6atac, U5, and U11
#=GF CC   snRNAs and associated proteins, forms a spliceosome that cleaves a
#=GF CC   divergent class of low-abundance pre-mRNA introns. Although the U12
#=GF CC   sequence is very divergent from that of U2 (Rfam:RF00004), the two are
#=GF CC   functionally analogous [2]. The predicted secondary structure of U12 RNA
#=GF CC   is published (see for example, PMID:10199569), but the alternative single
#=GF CC   hairpin in the 3' end shown here seems to better match the alignment of
#=GF CC   divergent Drosophila and Arabidopsis sequences.
#=GF WK   U12_minor_spliceosomal_RNA
#=GF SQ   62


