#=GF RT   The uRNA database.
#=GF RA   Zwieb C
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res 1997;25:102-103.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   10567566
#=GF RT   Nuclear retention elements of U3 small nucleolar RNA.
#=GF RA   Speckmann W, Narayanan A, Terns R, Terns MP
#=GF RL   Mol Cell Biol 1999;19:8412-8421.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   19875933
#=GF RT   Comparative analysis of eukaryotic U3 snoRNA.
#=GF RA   Marz M, Stadler PF
#=GF RL   RNA Biol. 2010;6:503-507.
#=GF CC   Small nucleolar RNAs (snoRNAs) are involved in the processing and
#=GF CC   modification of rRNA in the nucleolus. There are two main classes of
#=GF CC   snoRNAs: the box C/D class, and the box H/ACA class. U3 snoRNA is a member
#=GF CC   of the box C/D class. Indeed, the box C/D element is a subset of the six
#=GF CC   short sequence elements found in all U3 snoRNAs, namely boxes A, A', B, C,
#=GF CC   C', and D. The U3 snoRNA secondary structure is characterised by a small
#=GF CC   5' domain (with boxes A and A'), and a larger 3' domain (with boxes B, C,
#=GF CC   C', and D), the two domains being linked by a single-stranded hinge. Boxes
#=GF CC   B and C form the B/C motif, which appears to be exclusive to U3 snoRNAs,
#=GF CC   and boxes C' and D form the C'/D motif. The latter is functionally similar
#=GF CC   to the C/D motifs found in other snoRNAs. The 5' domain and the hinge
#=GF CC   region act as a pre-rRNA-binding domain. The 3' domain has conserved
#=GF CC   protein-binding sites. Both the box B/C and box C'/D motifs are sufficient
#=GF CC   for nuclear retention of U3 snoRNA. The box C'/D motif is also necessary
#=GF CC   for nucleolar localisation, stability and hyper-methylation of U3 snoRNA.
#=GF CC   Both box B/C and C'/D motifs are involved in specific protein interactions
#=GF CC   and are necessary for the rRNA processing functions of U3 snoRNA.
#=GF WK   Small_nucleolar_RNA_U3
#=GF SQ   87


