#=GF SM   cmsearch --cpu 4 --verbose --nohmmonly -T 30.00 -Z 742849.287494 CM SEQDB
#=GF DR   SO; 0000376; RNA_6S;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   10892648
#=GF RT   6S RNA regulates E. coli RNA polymerase activity.
#=GF RA   Wassarman KM, Storz G
#=GF RL   Cell. 2000;101:613-623.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   15793584
#=GF RT   A highly conserved 6S RNA structure is required for regulation of
#=GF RT   transcription.
#=GF RA   Trotochaud AE, Wassarman KM
#=GF RL   Nat Struct Mol Biol 2005;12:313-319.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   15811922
#=GF RT   6S RNA is a widespread regulator of eubacterial RNA polymerase that
#=GF RT   resembles an open promoter.
#=GF RA   Barrick JE, Sudarsan N, Weinberg Z, Ruzzo WL, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   RNA. 2005;11:774-784.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   28692405
#=GF RT   6S RNA in Rhodobacter sphaeroides: 6S RNA and pRNA transcript levels peak
#=GF RT   in late exponential phase and gene deletion causes a high salt stress
#=GF RT   phenotype.
#=GF RA   Elkina D, Weber L, Lechner M, Burenina O, Weisert A, Kubareva E, Hartmann
#=GF RA   RK, Klug G
#=GF RL   RNA Biol. 2017;17(11):1627-1637.
#=GF RN   [5]
#=GF RM   28988932
#=GF RT   6S RNA Mimics B-Form DNA to Regulate Escherichia coli RNA Polymerase
#=GF RA   Chen J, Wassarman KM, Feng A, Walz T, Campbell EA, Darst SA.
#=GF RL   Molecular Cell 2017;68:388-397.
#=GF CC   E. coli 6S RNA was the first non coding RNA to be sequenced, but its
#=GF CC   function was unknown until recently. It consists of 184 nucleotides that
#=GF CC   fold into an extended hairpin structure with a large single-stranded
#=GF CC   internal bulge. The 6S RNA specifically associates with RNA polymerase
#=GF CC   holoenzyme containing the sigma70 specificity factor. This interaction
#=GF CC   represses expression from a sigma70-dependent promoter during stationary
#=GF CC   phase [1]. 6S RNA homologs have recently been identified in most bacterial
#=GF CC   genomes [2,3]. Many Gram-positive species have two copies of 6S RNA. In
#=GF CC   Bacillus subtilis, both copies appear to interact with RNA polymerase
#=GF CC   holoenzyme containing the housekeeping sigma factor and be expressed
#=GF CC   during different stages of growth. In many proteobacteria, 6S RNA may be
#=GF CC   processed from a transcript encoding homologs of the E. coli YgfA protein
#=GF CC   which is a putative 5-formyltetrahydrofolate cycloligase activity.
#=GF CC   Structure of 6S-RNAP regulator has been reported in 5VT0 PDB [5]. 
#=GF WK   6S_/_SsrS_RNA
#=GF SQ   150


