#=GF RT   3' end processing of mouse histone pre-mRNA: evidence for additional
#=GF RT   base-pairing between U7 snRNA and pre-mRNA.
#=GF RA   Spycher C, Streit A, Stefanovic B, Albrecht D, Koning TH, Schumperli D
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res 1994;22:4023-4030.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   2825355
#=GF RT   Identification of the human U7 snRNP as one of several factors involved in
#=GF RT   the 3' end maturation of histone premessenger RNA's.
#=GF RA   Mowry KL, Steitz JA
#=GF RL   Science 1987;238:1682-1687.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   18267300
#=GF RT   U7 snRNAs: a computational survey.
#=GF RA   Marz M, Mosig A, Stadler BM, Stadler PF
#=GF RL   Genomics Proteomics Bioinformatics. 2007;5:187-195.
#=GF CC   Animal histone pre-mRNAs are spliced by a different mechanism than nuclear
#=GF CC   pre-mRNAs and self-splicing introns. This processing involves the U7
#=GF CC   snRNP, which contains only one RNA species: U7. The 5' end of U7 RNA is
#=GF CC   thought to base-pair to a conserved spacer element downstream of the
#=GF CC   cleavage site in histone pre-mRNA. This family contains a number of
#=GF CC   annotated U7 pseudogenes.
