#=GF CC   This family represents the plant microRNA (miRNA) precursor mir-166. This
#=GF CC   miRNA has now been predicted or experimentally confirmed in a wide range
#=GF CC   of plant species (MIPF:MIPF0000004). Animal miRNAs are transcribed as
#=GF CC   ~70nt precursors and subsequently processed by the Dicer enzyme to give a
#=GF CC   ~22nt product. In plants the precursor sequences may be longer, and the
#=GF CC   carpel factory (caf) enzyme appears to be involved in processing. In this
#=GF CC   case the mature sequence comes from the 3' arm of the precursor, and both
#=GF CC   Arabidopsis and rice genomes contain a number of related miRNA precursors
#=GF CC   which give rise to almost identical mature sequences. The extents of the
#=GF CC   hairpin precursors are not generally known and are estimated based on
#=GF CC   hairpin prediction. The products are thought to have regulatory roles
#=GF CC   through complementarity to mRNA.
#=GF WK   mir-166_microRNA_precursor
#=GF SQ   31



