#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   9032337
#=GF RT   Position dependence of functional hairpins important for human
#=GF RT   immunodeficiency virus type 1 RNA encapsidation in vivo.
#=GF RA   McBride MS, Panganiban AT
#=GF RL   J Virol 1997;71:2050-2058.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   9151848
#=GF RT   Efficient encapsidation of human immunodeficiency virus type 1 vectors and
#=GF RT   further characterization of cis elements required for encapsidation.
#=GF RA   McBride MS, Schwartz MD, Panganiban AT
#=GF RL   J Virol 1997;71:4544-4554.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   8627772
#=GF RT   The human immunodeficiency virus type 1 encapsidation site is a
#=GF RT   multipartite RNA element composed of functional hairpin structures.
#=GF RA   McBride MS, Panganiban AT
#=GF RL   J Virol 1996;70:2963-2973.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   12851400
#=GF RT   Rev binds specifically to a purine loop in the SL1 region of the HIV-1
#=GF RT   leader RNA.
#=GF RA   Gallego J, Greatorex J, Zhang H, Yang B, Arunachalam S, Fang J, Seamons J,
#=GF RA   Lea S, Pomerantz RJ, Lever AM
#=GF RL   J Biol Chem 2003;278:40385-40391.
#=GF RN   [5]
#=GF RM   12559920
#=GF RT   Structure of the intact stem and bulge of HIV-1 Psi-RNA stem-loop SL1.
#=GF RA   Lawrence DC, Stover CC, Noznitsky J, Wu Z, Summers MF
#=GF RL   J Mol Biol 2003;326:529-542.
#=GF RN   [6]
#=GF RM   10926523
#=GF RT   NMR structure of the HIV-1 nucleocapsid protein bound to stem-loop SL2 of
#=GF RT   the psi-RNA packaging signal. Implications for genome recognition.
#=GF RA   Amarasinghe GK, De Guzman RN, Turner RB, Chancellor KJ, Wu ZR, Summers MF
#=GF RL   J Mol Biol 2000;301:491-511.
#=GF RN   [7]
#=GF RM   9743628
#=GF RT   Three-dimensional folding of an RNA hairpin required for packaging HIV-1.
#=GF RA   Pappalardo L, Kerwood DJ, Pelczer I, Borer PN
#=GF RL   J Mol Biol 1998;282:801-818.
#=GF RN   [8]
#=GF RM   11724565
