#=GF DR   GO; 0051028; mRNA transport;
#=GF DR   GO; 0008298; intracellular mRNA localization;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   8582290
#=GF RT   A small predicted stem-loop structure mediates oocyte localization of
#=GF RT   Drosophila K10 mRNA.
#=GF RA   Serano TL, Cohen RS
#=GF RL   Development 1995;121:3809-3818.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   11533666
#=GF RT   A nuclear lamin is required for cytoplasmic organization and egg polarity
#=GF RT   in Drosophila.
#=GF RA   Guillemin K, Williams T, Krasnow MA
#=GF RL   Nat Cell Biol 2001;3:848-851.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   20473315
#=GF RT   A'-form RNA helices are required for cytoplasmic mRNA transport in
#=GF RT   Drosophila.
#=GF RA   Bullock SL, Ringel I, Ish-Horowicz D, Lukavsky PJ
#=GF RL   Nat Struct Mol Biol. 2010;17:703-709.
#=GF CC   This family represents the 44 nucleotide K10 transport/localisation
#=GF CC   element (TLS) from Drosophila melanogaster. K10 TLS is responsible for the
#=GF CC   transport and anterior localisation of K10 mRNA and acts to establish
#=GF CC   dorsoventral polarity in the oocyte [1]. K10 TLS structure was reported in
#=GF CC   the PDBs 2KE6, 2KUR, 2KUU, 2KUV, and 2KUW [3].
#=GF WK   K10_transport/localisation_element_%28TLS%29
#=GF SQ   10


