#=GF RT   The role of the pseudoknot at the 3' end of turnip yellow mosaic virus RNA
#=GF RT   in minus-strand synthesis by the viral RNA-dependent RNA polymerase.
#=GF RA   Deiman BA, Kortlever RM, Pleij CW
#=GF RL   J Virol 1997;71:5990-5996.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   15033563
#=GF RT   The tRNA-like structure of Turnip yellow mosaic virus RNA is a
#=GF RT   3'-translational enhancer.
#=GF RA   Matsuda D, Dreher TW
#=GF RL   Virology 2004;321:36-46.
#=GF CC   This family represents a pseudoknot structure from turnip yellow mosaic
#=GF CC   virus which is thought to be needed for efficient transcription as
#=GF CC   disruption of the pseudoknot structure gives rise to a 50% drop in
#=GF CC   transcription efficiency [1]. This family acts in conjunction with
#=GF CC   Rfam:RF00233 to enhance translation [2].
