#=GF CC   This family represents the related mir-15a and mir-15b sequences. In
#=GF CC   humans miR-15a and miR-16 are clustered within 0.5 kb at 13q14. This
#=GF CC   region has been shown to be deleted in more than half of B cell chronic
#=GF CC   lymphocytic leukaemias (CLL). Both miR-15a and miR-16 are deleted or
#=GF CC   down-regulated in more than two thirds of CLL cases [2]. The mature
#=GF CC   sequence is excised from the 5' arm of the hairpin. The family represents
#=GF CC   the microRNA (miRNA) precursor mir-125 imported from miRBase [3].
#=GF WK   mir-15_microRNA_precursor_family
#=GF SQ   164


