#=GF RA   McCormack JC, Simon AE
#=GF RL   J Virol 2004;78:7813-7817.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   15220437
#=GF RT   Repression and derepression of minus-strand synthesis in a plus-strand RNA
#=GF RT   virus replicon.
#=GF RA   Zhang G, Zhang J, Simon AE
#=GF RL   J Virol 2004;78:7619-7633.
#=GF CC   This family represents the turnip crinkle virus (TCV) hairpin 5 (H5) which
#=GF CC   contains a large symmetrical internal loop (LSL). H5 can repress
#=GF CC   minus-strand synthesis when the 3' side of the LSL pairs with the
#=GF CC   3'-terminal 4 bases of the RNA(GCCC-OH) [1,2].
