#=GF RL   RNA. 2002;8:125-128.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   10199569
#=GF RT   Conservation of functional features of U6atac and U12 snRNAs between
#=GF RT   vertebrates and higher plants.
#=GF RA   Shukla GC, Padgett RA
#=GF RL   RNA. 1999;5:525-538.
#=GF CC   U6atac is an essential component of the minor U12-type spliceosome complex
#=GF CC   which is required for removal of the rarer class of eukaryotic introns
#=GF CC   (AT-AC, U12-type) [1]. U6atac snRNA is proposed to form a base-paired
#=GF CC   complex with another spliceosomal RNA U4atac via two stem loop regions.
#=GF CC   These interacting stem loops have been shown to be required for in vivo
#=GF CC   splicing [2]. U6atac is the functional analog of U6 (Rfam:RF00026) in the
#=GF CC   major U2-type spliceosomal complex [2].
#=GF WK   U6atac_minor_spliceosomal_RNA
