#=GF RT   A genomewide search for ribozymes reveals an HDV-like sequence in the
#=GF RT   human CPEB3 gene.
#=GF RA   Salehi-Ashtiani K, Luptak A, Litovchick A, Szostak JW
#=GF RL   Science. 2006;313:1788-1792.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   15565159
#=GF RT   Autocatalytic RNA cleavage in the human beta-globin pre-mRNA promotes
#=GF RT   transcription termination.
#=GF RA   Teixeira A, Tahiri-Alaoui A, West S, Thomas B, Ramadass A, Martianov I,
#=GF RA   Dye M, James W, Proudfoot NJ, Akoulitchev A
#=GF RL   Nature. 2004;432:526-530.
#=GF CC   The mammalian CPEB3 ribozyme is a self cleaving RNA located in the second
#=GF CC   intron of the CPEB3 gene which belongs to a family of genes regulating
#=GF CC   messenger RNA polyadenylation [1]. This ribozyme is highly conserved and
#=GF CC   found only in mammals [1]. The CPEB3 ribozyme is structurally and
#=GF CC   biochemically related to the human hepatitis delta virus (HDV) ribozyme
#=GF CC   (Rfam:RF00094) and the HDV ribozyme is proposed to have arisen from the
#=GF CC   human transcriptome [1]. There is currently only one other known self
#=GF CC   cleaving ribozyme in mammals, the CoTC motif (Rfam:RF00621)[2].
#=GF WK   Mammalian_CPEB3_ribozyme
#=GF SQ   12


