#=GF RT   Confirmation of a second natural preQ1 aptamer class in Streptococcaceae
#=GF RT   bacteria.
#=GF RA   Meyer MM, Roth A, Chervin SM, Garcia GA, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   RNA. 2008;14:685-695.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   17621584
#=GF RT   Identification of 22 candidate structured RNAs in bacteria using the
#=GF RT   CMfinder comparative genomics pipeline.
#=GF RA   Weinberg Z, Barrick JE, Yao Z, Roth A, Kim JN, Gore J, Wang JX, Lee ER,
#=GF RA   Block KF, Sudarsan N, Neph S, Tompa M, Ruzzo WL, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res. 2007;35:4809-4819.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   24469808
#=GF RT   Structural determinants for ligand capture by a class II preQ1 riboswitch.
#=GF RA   Kang M, Eichhorn CD, Feigon J
#=GF RL   Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A. 2014;111:E663-E671.
#=GF CC   preQ1-II riboswitch was first reported for Weinberg et al. 2007 [7] it was
#=GF CC   recognised in Streptococcaceae and Lactococcus families in 5' untranslated
#=GF CC   regions of genes of a membrane protein classified as COG4708 or DUF988.
#=GF CC   Meyers et al. 2008 [1] confirm that preQ1-II recognise the queuosine (Q)
#=GF CC   precursor pre-queuosine 1 (preQ1). Q is a hyper modified nucleoside
#=GF CC   present in some anticodons in tRNAs (Try, Asn, Asp and His). The structure
#=GF CC   of preQ1-II riboswitch has been reported by Kang et al. 2014 [3], as preQ1
#=GF CC   riboswitch (RF00522) preQ1-II structure present an unusual H-type
#=GF CC   pseudoknot featuring and differs in the interactions that recognise preQ1.
#=GF CC   The structure of preQ1-II riboswitch was reported in PDB:2MIY [3]
#=GF WK   PreQ1-II_riboswitch
#=GF SQ   15


