#=GF DR   GO; 0010468; regulation of gene expression;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   20230605
#=GF RT   Comparative genomics reveals 104 candidate structured RNAs from bacteria,
#=GF RT   archaea and their metagenomes.
#=GF RA   Weinberg Z, Wang JX, Bogue J, Yang J, Corbino K, Moy RH, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Genome Biol. 2010;11:R31.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   28001372
#=GF RT   Biochemical Validation of a Third Guanidine Riboswitch Class in Bacteria.
#=GF RA   Sherlock ME, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Biochemistry. 2017;56:359-363.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   28988949
#=GF RT   Structure of the Guanidine III Riboswitch.
#=GF RA   Huang L, Wang J, Wilson TJ, Lilley DMJ
#=GF RL   Cell Chem Biol. 2017;24:1407-1415.
#=GF CC   Although the structure of ykkC-III RNAs does not resemble ykkC/yxkD RNAs,
#=GF CC   both have a structure complexity that led to the proposal that they
#=GF CC   represent riboswitches. The ykkC-III motif has a rigidly conserved ACGA
#=GF CC   sequence within it that resembles a less rigidly conserved ACGA or ACGG
#=GF CC   sequence found in mini-ykkC RNAs, but it is unknown whether this
#=GF CC   observation relates to a biological relationship. Biochemical validation
#=GF CC   has been presented to show that this motif is a third class of guanidine
#=GF CC   riboswitches [2]. The structure of Guanidine-III riboswitch has been
#=GF CC   reported in [3].
#=GF WK   YkkC-yxkD_leader
#=GF SQ   41


