#=GF CC   Potato leading responsible virus exoribonuclease-resistant RNA
#=GF CC   (PLRV-xrRNA) is a non-coding RNA (ncRNA) that blocks the progression of 5'
#=GF CC   to 3' exoribonuclease using only a folded RNA element, these elements were
#=GF CC   first reported in Flavivirus. Insights into the mechanism of programmed
#=GF CC   exoribonuclease resistance in PLRV has been reported using X-ray
#=GF CC   crystallography and in vitro assays of exoribonuclease resistance [1,2].
#=GF CC   The structure of PLRV_xrRNA is reported in PDB 7JJU [1]
#=GF WK   Flavivirus_3'_UTR
